        "original_id": "9843516d-4473-50fa-a5c1-723b2f8f2210",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Peter Staley\n- Products: How to Survive a Plague\n- Places: St. Patrick's Cathedral (Manhattan), New York City\n- Events: 1989 demonstration during mass at St. Patrick's Cathedral, September 21, 2012 U.S. theatrical opening\n- Concepts: Neo-Gothic-style Roman Catholic cathedral church\n\nFacts:\n- In 1989, a demonstration took place during mass at St. Patrick's Cathedral.\n- On September 21, 2012, the film How to Survive a Plague opened in select theatres across the United States.\n- How to Survive a Plague includes footage of the 1989 demonstration during mass at St. Patrick's Cathedral.\n- Peter Staley is a primary figure in the Oscar-nominated documentary How to Survive a Plague.\n- St. Patrick's Cathedral, commonly called St. Patrick's Cathedral, is a decorated Neo-Gothic-style Roman Catholic cathedral church in the United States and a prominent landmark of New York City.",
